@startuml lid-close
' THE SOURCE OF TRUTH for what Insomnia does, and what it sounds like, when the
' lid closes and when the battery runs out (Victor, 2026-10-14).
'
' Bound to the code by LidRulesDiagramTests:
'   - every **name** in an action box is a LidAwakePolicy.Action case, and back;
'   - every 🔊 **name** is a LidAwakePolicy.Sound case, and back;
'   - every decision's inputs are the parameters of LidAwakePolicy.decide /
'     soundOnLidClose / soundOnTick, and each path through here is one row of
'     LidRulesDiagramTests.paths.
' Change a rule here first, then the policy, then the row.
'
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/lid-close.puml  (or -tpng)

title Insomnia — lid close & battery floor: what happens, what is heard

skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #FDFDFD
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF6D5
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
skinparam ArrowColor #444444

start

switch (what happened?)

' ─────────────────────────────── the lid comes down ───────────────────────────
case ( lid closed\n(a real open→closed edge,\nnot a dark wake) )

  if (armed, on battery, floor ticked,\nbattery < 20%?) then (yes)
    :**standDown**
    mode → Off, flag off, 🪫 overlay; <<#FFE0E0>>
  elseif (armed and (Always, or a Claude working\nwith internet in the last 5 min)?) then (yes)
    if (on battery?) then (yes)
      :**beat**
      hold the flag; <<#E0FFE0>>
    else (no — on AC)
      :**hold**
      hold the flag; <<#E0FFE0>>
    endif
  elseif (armed, we were holding, and nothing\nelse keeps the shut lid up?) then (yes)
    :**farewell**
    the flag stays up for the sound; <<#FFF0D0>>
  else (no)
    :**release**
    nothing was held; <<#EEEEEE>>
  endif

  if (does the Mac stay up?\n(a Claude/Always holds it, an external display,\nor SleepDisabled raised by someone else)) then (yes)
    :🔊 **threeQuickBeats**
    three lub-dubs: "I am staying up"; <<#C8F7C8>>
    note right
      on battery the 💓 heartbeat
      then carries on every 10 s
    end note
  else (no — it is going to sleep)
    :🔊 **flatTone**
    only the flatline's long tone —
    never the dying pulse on a lid close
    (flag held up ≤ 3 s so the tone plays); <<#D0E4FF>>
    :pmset sleepnow;
  endif

' ─────────────────────────── the 10-second tick ───────────────────────────────
case ( every 10 s,\nwhile armed )

  if (on battery, floor ticked,\nbattery < 20%?) then (yes)
    :**standDown**
    mode → Off, flag off, 🪫 overlay; <<#FFE0E0>>
    if (lid closed?) then (yes)
      :🔊 **dyingPulse**
      three Bassos, then the whole 🫀 flatline; <<#FFB0B0>>
      :the Mac sleeps;
    else (no — open)
      :🔊 **none**
      the overlay says it; <<#EEEEEE>>
    endif
  elseif (Always, or a Claude working\nwith internet in the last 5 min?) then (yes)
    if (lid closed and on battery?) then (yes)
      :**beat**
      hold the flag; <<#E0FFE0>>
      :🔊 **heartbeat**
      one lub-dub
      (three quick ones on the first beat); <<#C8F7C8>>
    else (no)
      :**hold**
      hold the flag; <<#E0FFE0>>
      :🔊 **none**; <<#EEEEEE>>
    endif
  elseif (we were holding, and the lid is closed\nwith nothing else keeping the Mac up?) then (yes)
    :**farewell**
    the work finished (or the internet
    has been gone ≥ 5 min) under the lid; <<#FFF0D0>>
    if (on battery?) then (yes)
      :🔊 **dyingPulse**
      the whole 🫀 flatline:
      two last beats, then the long tone; <<#FFB0B0>>
    else (no — on AC, no external display)
      :🔊 **flatTone**
      only the long tone; <<#D0E4FF>>
    endif
    :flag off, pmset sleepnow;
  else (no)
    :**release**
    flag off — the Mac may sleep,
    the mode stays armed; <<#EEEEEE>>
    :🔊 **none**; <<#EEEEEE>>
  endif

endswitch

stop

legend right
  The dying pulse is reserved for one thing: the Mac is **on battery**,
  the lid is **already closed**, and then the work finishes or the
  battery crosses the floor. Closing the lid never plays it — a lid close
  that ends in sleep plays only the **flat tone**, whatever the reason
  (no work, work just finished, battery already low, mode Off, on AC).
endlegend

@enduml
